            "_comment": "Profile 0 - remote/external monitor BELOW the laptop (current default). CONFIG_VERSION 11 affine drag gain: drag_gain = base*1000, drag_curve_k = slope*1e4; per-flush gain(v) = base + slope*v (v=|rx|+|ry|), clamped to ~1.3 in firmware, modelling macOS drag accel. Local Mac (output 0) SETTLED at base 260, slope 390. Tuning path: 260/430 over-advanced and the over-advance GREW with drag size (+39px moderate rightward, +164px large up-left) = the SLOPE term overshooting macOS's concave gain at the higher speeds a large drag reaches; base (slow drags) was fine. Cutting slope only: 430->370 over-corrected (backward rebound), 430->390 centres the residual on zero - a drag now lands a hair forward or back depending on its exact speed (macOS uses smoothed velocity; per-flush affine can't track that, so the residual has no fixed sign). 390 is the practical floor for config tuning. Isolate base (slow) from slope (fast) when tuning; the earlier whole-line cuts (250/400, 440/170) failed because they dropped base too. Trust merge.py's H/F ratio, NOT analyze_curve's per-flush gain fit. Remote (output 1) reuses the local estimate, validate separately. Tune live with make apply-config.",
